Rule 6 (target tensor elements should be between 0 and 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 7 (Input tensor can have arbitrary shape, but must be a tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 10 (Input and Target tensors must have compatible shapes for broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : (if ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0 then true else if ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0 then true else shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1)
>>
Rule 13 (Target tensor must have floating point dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 15 (reduction parameter is valid even if input/target are empty)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1]: shape(v_2, i) = 0) ∨ (v_3 = "none" ∨ v_3 = "mean" ∨ v_3 = "sum")
>>
Rule 18 (Target tensor values must be between 0 and 1 inclusive.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) ∧ min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 20 (reduction parameter should not be none when both input and target have more than zero dimensions)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor, v_3: str} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1]: shape(v_2, i) = 0) ∨ v_3 ≠ "none"
>>
Rule 25 (If reduction is "none", the output tensor should have the same shape as the input tensor.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if v_3 = "none" then (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
